  "body_markdown": "## Microsoft Security Advisory CVE-2026-118740 - Aspire Security Feature Bypass Vulnerability\n\nSource-reported by [GitHub Security Advisories](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-4g86-54fm-h9h8).\n\nCVE-2026-118740 (official CVSS 9.1): Missing authorization in Aspire allows an unauthorized attacker to bypass a security feature over a network.\n\n**What to do:** Upgrade to a fixed release: Aspire.Dashboard.Sdk.linux-x64 13.6.5, Aspire.Dashboard.Sdk.linux-arm64 13.6.5, Aspire.Dashboard.Sdk.linux-musl-x64 13.6.5, Aspire.Dashboard.Sdk.osx-x64 13.6.5, Aspire.Dashboard.Sdk.osx-arm64 13.6.5, Aspire.Dashboard.Sdk.win-x64 13.6.5, Aspire.Dashboard.Sdk.win-arm64 13.6.5.\n\n| Claim | Check | Source |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| CVE-2026-118740 exists | confirmed | [cve.org](https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-118740) |\n| CVSS 9.1 | official | [NVD](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-118740) |\n\nIdentifiers and scores checked automatically against cve.org and NVD.\n\n**Limitations:** Source-reported; SecOpsAI did not reproduce the issue.\n\nPublished 12 Nov 2026, 17:17 UTC; first seen by SecOpsAI 12 Nov 2026, 17:22 UTC.\n\n## Collection scope\n\nSecOpsAI watched 29 sources for this edition; all were current. 5 package registries are watched through release metadata only, without scanning package contents. This is not complete coverage of every source or registry.\n\n## Credits and corrections\n\nPrepared by Onyedika Christopher Agada. The editor approves each edition before it is published. Corrections keep the previous edition and explain material changes.",
